  "market_context": "During a strong uptrend on the DAX 1-hour chart, price made consecutive higher highs while RSI formed lower highs, signaling loss of bullish momentum. The reversal occurred after two rejection candles at the peak, confirmed by a break of the downtrend line drawn from prior swing lows.",
  "key_observation": "Price made a higher high near 15444.75 while RSI showed a lower high (RSI ~69.51), forming a regular bearish divergence; two rejection candles appeared at that high, triggering the short entry.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified a regular bearish divergence on the DAX 1-hour chart where price created a higher high but RSI formed a lower high.",
    "Step 2: Observed two consecutive rejection candles at the recent high (near 15444.75), confirming loss of upward momentum.",
    "Step 3: Drew a trend line connecting prior swing lows and noted price broke below it, confirming trend reversal structure.",
    "Step 4: Entered a short position at the close of the second rejection candle with stop loss above the prior swing high.",
    "Step 5: Targeted a 1:2 risk-to-reward ratio, capturing a 100-point move for $100 profit on 0.01 lots."
  ],
  "outcome": "100-point move captured, $100 profit on 0.01 lots with 1:2 R:R",
  "lessons": "Regular bearish divergences are most reliable when combined with visible price rejection (e.g., two rejection candles) and structural confirmation (e.g., trend line break). Always wait for candle close before entry to avoid false breakouts.",
